@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+**P-310. Context manager placement and names; P-310 adds to the P-15 name map.** TS exports the context manager from `@strands-agents/sdk/experimental` (`context-manager/`). Choice: `strands::experimental::context_manager` (re-exported at `strands::experimental`) with private `methods::truncate`, `presets`, `retrieval_tool`, `search` (the port of `vended-plugins/context-offloader/search.ts`, crate-internal), `stash`, crate-internal `modes::agentic`, and public `strategies::offload::{base, drop, emergency, summarize, truncate}` re-exported at the module root. Types: `ContextManager` (`new(ContextManagerConfig) -> Result`, `from_preset`, `from_strategy` for TS `ContextManager.from`, `NAME`, `strategy_names`, `stash() -> Option<&Stash>`, `stash_is_durable`), `ContextManagerConfig { strategies: Option<Vec<ContextStrategyEntry>>, stash: Option<StashOption> }`, `StashConfig { storage, retrieval_tool: bool (default true) }`, `StashOption::{Enabled(StashConfig), Disabled}` (TS `StashConfig | boolean`, `From<bool>`), `ContextStrategyEntry::{Strategy, Preset}` (TS `ContextStrategy | StrategyPresetName`), `StrategyPresetName` enum with `FromStr` (TS error text) and `STRATEGY_PRESET_NAMES`, `ContextManagerPreset::{Auto, Agentic}` with `FromStr` (TS `Unknown contextManager preset` text), `ContextManagerStrategy::{Preset, Config, Manager(Arc<ContextManager>), Off}` (TS `ContextManagerStrategy`; `Off` is TS `false`), `ContextState<'a> { agent, utilization, overflow, stash, invocation_context }` with `new`, `messages`, `messages_mut` (TS `messages` and `agent` alias the same history, so Rust keeps only `agent`), `OffloadTarget::{All, ToolResults, ToolResultErrors, AssistantText, UserText, Tools(Vec<String>)}`, `OffloadConditions { threshold, utilization, preserve_recent }` (all `Option<f64>`, TS numbers), `TruncateConfig { preview_tokens: Option<u64>, preview: Option<PreviewMode> }`, `PreviewMode::{Head, Tail, HeadTail}`, `SummarizeConfig { model, system_prompt }`, `Offload` (unit struct; `drop`, `truncate`, `summarize` return `Result` because TS throws on an empty array target; `.when(..)` consumes and returns `Result` because `TruncateStrategy` throws on `threshold <= previewTokens`), `DropStrategy`, `TruncateStrategy`, `SummarizeStrategy`, `EmergencyTruncateStrategy` (`NAME`), `DROPPED_MARKER`, `BLOCK_SUMMARY_INSTRUCTIONS`, `RETRIEVAL_TOOL_NAME`, `Stash` (`new(storage, session_id, agent_id, custom_namespace: bool)` for TS `{ customStashNamespace }`, `storage_type_name`, `is_durable`, `store`, `refs_for`, `store_message`, `retrieve -> Option<JsonValue>` for TS `{ data } | null`, `list`, `delete`, `clear`, `clear_session`, `take_snapshot`, `load_snapshot`). Agent: `AgentConfig::context_manager: Option<ContextManagerStrategy>`, `Agent::context_manager()`, `LocalAgent::session_id()`. TS reference: `context-manager/{context-manager,types,presets,stash,retrieval-tool}.ts`, `strategies/offload/*.ts`, `agent/agent.ts:345-367,584,612-641,693-704`. Files: `src/experimental.rs`, `src/experimental/context_manager*`.
+
+**P-311. `ContextStrategy` shape.** TS `ContextStrategy` has `name`, optional sync `init(agent, stash?)` and async `apply(context)`. Choice: `#[async_trait] trait ContextStrategy: Send + Sync + 'static { fn name(&self) -> &str; fn init(self: Arc<Self>, agent: &mut LocalAgent, stash: Option<Stash>) {} async fn apply(&self, context: &mut ContextState<'_>) -> Result<bool>; }`; `init` takes `Arc<Self>` so eager strategies can register a `MessageAddedEvent` hook that holds themselves. Strategy state TS keeps in fields (`_stash`) sits behind a `Mutex`. The runner's TS `instanceof EmergencyTruncateStrategy` check compares `name()` with `EmergencyTruncateStrategy::NAME`, since the public API never downcasts. The offload strategies share crate-internal `OffloadBase` plus an `Offloader` trait (`base`, `removal_marker`, `replace_block`) in place of the TS abstract class; message identity (`indexOf`) becomes indices. TS reference: `context-manager/types.ts:21-36`, `strategies/offload/base.ts`. Files: `src/experimental/context_manager.rs`, `src/experimental/context_manager/strategies/offload/base.rs`.
+
+**P-312. Agentic tools edit history through the tool batch.** TS `summarize_context`, `truncate_context` and `pin_context` splice `context.agent.messages` in place; Rust tools see `ToolAgent`, whose history is a snapshot (P-48). Choice: a crate-internal history-edit slot on `ToolAgent` (`replace_messages`, `current_messages`, `take_history_edit`); the loop applies the last edit to `LocalAgent` after the executor finishes and before `AfterToolsEvent`, so the assistant tool-use message and results are appended to the edited history, as in TS's deferred append. A later tool in the same batch reads the edit through `current_messages`; concurrent edits in one batch keep the last writer. TS reference: `context-manager/modes/agentic/agentic-context.ts:75-311`. Files: `src/types/agent.rs`, `src/agent/run.rs`, `src/experimental/context_manager/modes/agentic.rs`.
+
+**P-313. Stash `storageType` from a hidden `Storage::storage_type_name`.** TS writes `storage.constructor.name`. Choice: `#[doc(hidden)] fn storage_type_name(&self) -> &'static str` on `Storage`, defaulting to the implementing type's name without its path (`InMemoryStorage`, `LocalFileStorage`, or a custom backend's struct name), and `"Object"` for the generic namespaced view (TS's view is an object literal). Built-in `namespace()` views keep their class name, as in TS. TS reference: `context-manager/stash.ts:82`, `storage/storage.ts:193-212`. Files: `src/storage.rs`, `src/experimental/context_manager/stash.rs`.
+
+**P-314. Agent session id.** TS `agent.sessionId` is the session manager's id, else `crypto.randomUUID().slice(0, 8)`. Choice: `LocalAgent::session_id()`, set in `Agent::new` from the session manager, else the last 8 hex digits of a UUID v7 (its random bits; the first 8 are the timestamp). TS reference: `agent/agent.ts:524-533`. Files: `src/types/agent.rs`, `src/agent/agent.rs`.
+
+**P-315. Truncation previews count characters.** TS `buildPreview` and the retrieval caps use `string.length` (UTF-16 code units). Choice: Rust counts and slices by `char` (section 7.3), so a preview never splits a surrogate pair; ASCII output is identical, and the token estimate (`ceil(chars / 4)`) differs only for non-BMP text. TS reference: `context-manager/methods/truncate.ts:33-69`, `retrieval-tool.ts:71-76`, `vended-plugins/context-offloader/search.ts:21-26`. Files: `src/experimental/context_manager/methods/truncate.rs`, `search.rs`, `retrieval_tool.rs`.
+
+**P-316. Strategy-runner failures are logged.** TS `_runStrategies` counts the history outside its try, so a failing `countTokens` rejects the hook and fails the model call. Rust hooks can't return errors; the runner logs `context reduction failed` and the call proceeds (overflow recovery then reports no progress). Per-strategy failures are logged and skipped, as in TS. TS reference: `context-manager/context-manager.ts:205-244`. Files: `src/experimental/context_manager.rs`.
+
+**P-317. Summarize strategy details.** Block token counts call `agent.model().count_tokens` directly (TS calls `agent.model.countTokens` per block and `ModelProxy.countTokens` for the whole history; the Rust `ModelProxy` has no `count_tokens`). Log lines name the model by `model_id()` where TS prints `model.constructor.name`. `SummarizeOptions.agent_metadata` is not passed because the loop doesn't carry agent metadata yet (P-304). Usage of summary calls is recorded on the auxiliary invocation context as in TS. TS reference: `strategies/offload/summarize.ts`. Files: `src/experimental/context_manager/strategies/offload/summarize.rs`.
+
+**P-318. `retrieve_context` patterns use the `regex` crate.** TS compiles the pattern with `new RegExp` and falls back to an escaped literal on a syntax error or a nested quantifier. Rust compiles with `regex::Regex` (no backreferences or lookaround; linear time) with the same nested-quantifier check and `regex::escape` fallback. TS reference: `vended-plugins/context-offloader/search.ts:41-60`. Files: `src/experimental/context_manager/search.rs`.
+
+**P-319. `pin_context` validates without `action` required.** `z.toJSONSchema` lists `action` (which has `.default('pin')`) in `required`, but Zod's parse fills the default, so TS accepts input without it. Rust sends the TS schema unchanged and validates against a copy whose `required` is `["select"]`; serde fills the default. The four tool schemas were generated with the repo's Zod and are asserted in tests. TS reference: `modes/agentic/agentic-context.ts:183-207`. Files: `src/experimental/context_manager/modes/agentic.rs`.
+
+**P-320. Edits outside the context manager paths.** `storage.rs` (P-313), `types/agent.rs` (session id, context stash slot, `ToolAgent` history edit), `types/snapshot.rs` (`Snapshot::data_mut`, crate-internal), `agent/config.rs` (`context_manager` key), `agent/agent.rs` (TS `resolveConversationManager`, the agentic tools and token-usage middleware, the context manager in the registration order after delegation and before the session manager, `Agent::context_manager()`, `registration_order` made crate-internal for tests), `agent/run.rs` (P-312), `session/session_manager.rs` (TS `_includeStashData`, `_restoreStashData`, `_deleteStashData`), `conversation_manager/token_usage_middleware.rs` (`grouped` made crate-internal), `lib.rs` (`pub mod experimental`). TS reference: `agent/agent.ts`, `session/session-manager.ts:184,224,236,273,350-394`. Files: those listed.
diff --git a/.rust-port/staging/phase6c/divergences.md b/.rust-port/staging/phase6c/divergences.md
